  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Peraton has $1.8B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date, across 261 awards with an average award size of $6.7M. Obligations fell 16.1% year over year. The General Services Administration is the largest buyer with $650M, followed by the Department of Defense with $359M and the Department of Transportation with $210M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market for Peraton with $862M, and Engineering Services is the second-largest with $380M. FY2026 obligations of $1.8B follow a sequence of annual obligations: FY21 $466M, FY22 $1.1B, FY23 $1.7B, FY24 $2B, and FY25 $2.1B. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration accounts for $183M in FY2026 to date, and the Department of Health and Human Services accounts for $113M. Smaller agency relationships include the Department of State at $86.9M and the Department of Commerce at $86.1M. The FY2026 data are partial, reflecting fiscal year to date totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How do Peraton obligations in FY2026 compare to recent years?",
        "body": "Peraton obligated $1.8B in FY2026 to date, down 16.1% year over year. Peraton recorded FY25 obligations of $2.1B and FY24 obligations of $2B, with FY23 at $1.7B, FY22 at $1.1B, and FY21 at $466M. The current-year total is a fiscal year to date figure, not a full-year total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and markets drive Peraton's FY2026 obligations?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration obligated $650M and the Department of Defense obligated $359M in FY2026 to date. Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $862M and Engineering Services accounted for $380M in FY2026 to date. Other notable markets include Custom Computer Programming Services at $152M and Other Computer Related Services at $121M."
      }
    ]
  },
